        "comments": "Mobiluncus curtisii ATCC 43063\n\nStrain source, body site: Urogenital tract, vagina\n\nInquiries should be directed to microbe@hgsc.bcm.tmc.edu\n\nThis sequence is an upgraded sequence that has been subjected to automatic finishing procedures including computational calculation with experimental execution of directed PCR experiments to order and orient many of the whole genome shotgun sequence contigs. The automatic finishing was followed by further experiments to fully order and orient the contigs within the genome and clarify the remaining ambiguous sequence. This sequence meets the quality standards for HMP grade (HTGS_PHASE3).\n\nThis is a reference genome for the Human Microbiome Project. This project is co-owned with the Human Microbiome Project DACC. Source DNA provided by Sheldon Kaplan (Texas Children's Hospital, Department of Pediatric Infectious Diseases, 1102 Bates Street #1150, Houston, TX, 77030). Bacteria provided by ATCC (43063), funded by \"Genomes and Genetics at the BCM-HGSC\" (U54 HG003273).\nThe annotation was added by the NCBI Prokaryotic Genome Annotation Pipeline (PGAP). Information about PGAP can be found here: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genome/annotation_prok/",
